  "content": {
    "id": "p57-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "",
    "prompt": "A farmer has 400 metres of fencing to construct a rectangular field.\nOne of the sides is a river, so the farmer only needs to fence three sides of the rectangle.\nThe farmer wants to use all the fencing available to make the largest possible area.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p57-q7-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 57 p57-q7-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black}]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (0,0)--(0,2)--(4,2)--(4,0);\n\\node[left] at (0,1) {$x$};\n\\node[above] at (2,2) {$y$};\n\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (-0.8,0) .. controls (-0.4,0.06) and (-0.2,-0.06) .. (0.2,0) .. controls (0.8,0.06) and (1.2,-0.06) .. (1.8,0) .. controls (2.4,0.06) and (2.8,-0.06) .. (3.4,0) .. controls (4,0.06) and (4.4,-0.06) .. (4.8,0);\n\\node[below] at (2,-0.1) {River};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
        "widthMm": 70,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
        "axes": null,
        "spec": {
          "sourcePage": 57,
          "sourceRegion": "Question 7: diagram beneath the shared stem",
          "description": "Three fenced sides of an unshaded rectangular field meet a river along the unfenced bottom side. The river is explicitly labelled to retain its identity without decorative fill.",
          "mathematics": "The two sides perpendicular to the river each have length x; the fenced side parallel to the river has length y. No numerical lengths or scale are supplied.",
          "answerVisibility": "Permanent student given."
        },
        "derived": false,
        "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
      }
    ],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p57-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that we can model this situation as $2x+y=400$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The fenced sides total $x+y+x=400$, so $2x+y=400$.",
          "worked": "The three fenced sides have lengths $x$, $y$ and $x$ metres, and all 400 metres of fencing are used.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+y+x&=400\\\\2x+y&=400\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Show that the area of the field is $A=400x-2x^2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$A=xy=x(400-2x)=400x-2x^2$.",
          "worked": "From part (a), $y=400-2x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=xy\\\\A&=x(400-2x)\\\\A&=400x-2x^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "By completing the square of the above expression, or otherwise, find the maximum area of the field that the farmer can construct.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$20\\,000\\text{ m}^2$, since $A=-2(x-100)^2+20\\,000$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A&=400x-2x^2\\\\A&=-2(x^2-200x)\\\\A&=-2\\bigl((x-100)^2-10\\,000\\bigr)\\\\A&=-2(x-100)^2+20\\,000\\end{align*}$$\nSince $(x-100)^2\\geq0$, the maximum turning point is $(100,20\\,000)$. The maximum area is $20\\,000\\text{ m}^2$.\n\nAlternatively, the parabola is concave down and its vertex occurs at\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=-\\frac{b}{2a}\\\\x&=-\\frac{400}{2(-2)}\\\\x&=100.\\end{align*}$$\nSubstituting into the area model,\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=400(100)-2(100)^2\\\\A&=20\\,000\\text{ m}^2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      }
    ]
  },
